  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Eradicating violence against women and girls - Tanzania</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This intervention (known as SASA!) takes local communities through a four-stage process of increasing knowledge, changing attitudes and norms, and finally altering behaviour to decrease the prevalence of intimate partner violence against women and HIV. It is implemented in the Kigoma and Mwanza regions of Tanzania by Women&apos;s Promotion Centre and Kivulini.</narrative>
  </description>
